# date-toto — Project Overview

## What This Project Is

`date-toto` is a faithful CLI replica of the GNU Core Utilities `date` command.
It displays, formats, and converts date and time information to stdout — a single
formatted line ending in a newline — then exits.

Formatting is done by a self-implemented `%` directive engine and civil-date/epoch
arithmetic (C locale only). libc supplies only the current instant
(`clock_gettime`), the local UTC offset, and the timezone abbreviation. No
`strftime`.

## Binary Name

The compiled binary must always be named **`date-toto`**. Never rename it.
On Windows, MinGW may also emit `date-toto.exe`; that is the same program.

## Platforms

| Platform | Build environment | Notes |
|----------|-------------------|-------|
| **Linux** | `gcc`/`clang` + GNU Make | Full POSIX path: `sigaction(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN)` |
| **Windows** | **MSYS2 UCRT64** (recommended) | Native Windows `.exe`; `install_sigpipe_ignore()` is a no-op under `_WIN32` |
| **Git Bash** | Works if `/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is **early** on `PATH` | Same binary as UCRT64; see `toolchain-structure.mdc` |

Binaries are **not portable** across OSes — build separately on Linux and on Windows.

## Scope — Keep It Minimal

Supporting behaviour:

- Bare `date-toto` — default format (GNU-like: `%a %b %e %H:%M:%S %Z %Y`)
- `+FORMAT` operand — self-implemented conversion directives
- `-u` / `--utc` / `--universal` — use UTC
- `-d` / `--date=STRING` — display a date described by STRING (ISO-ish + simple relative)
- `-r` / `--reference=FILE` — use the referenced file's modification time
- `-I` / `--iso-8601[=FMT]` — ISO 8601-style output
- `-R` / `--rfc-email` — RFC 5322-style output
- Built-in `--help` / `--h` and `--version` / `--v` (detected anywhere in `argv`; help wins if both appear)

**Do not add**:

- Clock setting (`-s` / `--set`, `MMDDhhmm[[CC]YY][.ss]` operand)
- `-f` / `--file=DATEFILE`
- `--debug`
- Locales beyond C (weekday/month names are English, fixed)
- Sub-second `%N` and GNU padding/flag modifiers (`%-`, `%_`, `%^`, field widths)
- Interactive or TUI modes
- stdin reading (except what `-r` does via the filesystem)
- Logging or debug output in normal operation
- Single-dash `-h` / `-v` (only `--help`, `--h`, `--version`, and `--v` are special among those forms)
- Any feature that would break GNU `date` behavioural compatibility within the supported subset

## Behavioural Contract

| Invocation | Output / behaviour |
|---|---|
| `date-toto` | prints current local date/time in the default format, one line + `\n`, exits `0` |
| `date-toto +%Y-%m-%d` | prints formatted date (e.g. `2026-09-06\n`), exits `0` |
| `date-toto +%s` | prints Unix timestamp (seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC), exits `0` |
| `date-toto -u` / `date-toto --utc` | same as default, but in UTC (`%Z` → `UTC`) |
| `date-toto -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'` | UTC with custom format |
| `date-toto -d tomorrow` / `date-toto --date=tomorrow` | formats the described instant |
| `date-toto -d '7 days ago' +%F` | relative date + format |
| `date-toto -r FILE` / `date-toto --reference=FILE` | formats the file's mtime |
| `date-toto -I` / `date-toto --iso-8601` | ISO 8601 date (date precision) |
| `date-toto -Iseconds` / `date-toto --iso-8601=seconds` | ISO 8601 with seconds + offset |
| `date-toto -R` / `date-toto --rfc-email` | RFC 5322-style date line |
| `date-toto --version` / `date-toto --v` | prints `date-toto <version>\n`, exits `0` |
| `date-toto --help` / `date-toto --h` | prints usage on stdout, exits `0` |
| `date-toto +%Y \| head -c 4` | may exit `0` on broken pipe (`EPIPE`) |

## Exit Codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `0` | Successful print, `--help`, `--version`, or broken pipe (`EPIPE` on `write`) |
| `1` | Invalid option, invalid date string, unreadable `-r` file, other `write()` failure, OOM formatting, or signal setup failure |

